Files that came from elsewhere
------------------------------

A few files were written by other people and are kept under the terms they came
with. They are the exception, and each one says so in its own header. Read the
header, not this file, if the two ever disagree.

    uniswap/src/vendor/ABDKMathQuad.sol
        BSD-4-Clause, (c) 2019 ABDK Consulting. IEEE 754 binary128 in software.
        Vendored to be measured, not used: it is what makes Uniswap's TWAMM cost
        what it does.

    uniswap/script/bench/vendor/StylusDeployer.sol
        MIT, Offchain Labs. `cargo stylus` routes CREATE2 deployments through it,
        and it exists only on real Arbitrum chains, so the benchmarks need a copy.

    uniswap/test/utils/libraries/EasyPosm.sol
        GPL-2.0-or-later. A Uniswap v4 test helper.

    uniswap/test/utils/Deployers.sol
    uniswap/test/utils/BaseTest.sol
        No licence stated upstream. Uniswap v4 test helpers.

Everything under uniswap/lib/ is a git submodule. Those are separate repositories
and carry their own licences; nothing here relicenses them.


What is not in here
-------------------

No copyleft or source-available code is reproduced in the parts of this repository
that ship. Uniswap's own TwammMath is marked UNLICENSED and is not used: both
uniswap/src/TwammHook.sol and stylus/native-twamm implement the published closed
form (Paradigm, 2021) from the formula. EulerSwap is BUSL-1.1 and is referenced in
BENCHMARK.md for information, with none of its code copied.
